    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a1">

                <pb facs="0159" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg125"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Henriques to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dominican Republic,<lb/>Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November
                                5, 1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: The Government of the Dominican
                    Republic, of which I am a representative, has authorized me to address that of
                    the United States of America, through the worthy medium of your excellency, in
                    order to notify it of the denunciation of the treaty of friendship, commerce,
                    and navigation entered into between the two Governments the 8th day of February,
                    1867.</p>
                <p>In obeying these instructions, I must tell your excellency that this denunciation
                    is based upon Article XXXI of the treaty, and that its object is, therefore, to
                    terminate its effects.</p>
                <p>I consequently take pleasure in informing your excellency that the Dominican
                    Government entertains the hope that the treaty of 1867 will, at no distant day,
                    be replaced by conventions in every respect suited to the present needs of both
                    countries.</p>
                <p>With this hope, and cherishing the warmest wishes for the stability and greatness
                    of the United States, I have the honor, Mr. Minister, to subscribe myself, your
                    excellency’s most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henrique
                    Henriques.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
